1
00:01:30,719 --> 00:01:54,663
I don't believe it!

2
00:01:54,663 --> 00:01:56,807
What's wrong?

3
00:01:56,807 --> 00:01:59,118
Carter Boswell!

4
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:00,398
Who's Carter Boswell?

5
00:02:00,398 --> 00:02:02,096
He's running for the school board.

6
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:03,096
The election's next month.

7
00:02:03,096 --> 00:02:05,074
What's wrong with wanting to be on the school board?

8
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:05,574
Nothing.

9
00:02:05,574 --> 00:02:09,642
But he wants to cut the school budget!

10
00:02:09,642 --> 00:02:11,522
Maybe it needs cutting.

11
00:02:11,522 --> 00:02:14,008
Cutting the budget is fine,

12
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:15,508
but he wants to do it

13
00:02:15,508 --> 00:02:16,986
by cutting all the cultural programs.

14
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:18,486
No music, no dance,

15
00:02:18,486 --> 00:02:20,339
no concert, no stage presentations.

16
00:02:20,339 --> 00:02:22,942
Why does he want to do that?

17
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,920
He says it's to save the taxpayers' money,

18
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:27,170
and I think he believes

19
00:02:27,170 --> 00:02:28,898
that the taxpayers will vote for him

20
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:31,876
if he spends less on the cultural programs.

21
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:33,876
He's probably right.

22
00:02:33,876 --> 00:02:35,927
Lots of people want their taxes

23
00:02:35,927 --> 00:02:37,357
used for new books

24
00:02:37,357 --> 00:02:40,512
and a new paint job in the schoolrooms.

25
00:02:40,512 --> 00:02:42,770
Maybe some of us would like to pay a little bit more

26
00:02:42,770 --> 00:02:45,788
and keep the cultural programs for our kids.

27
00:02:45,788 --> 00:02:48,766
Well, I'm not sure. Ellen.

28
00:02:48,766 --> 00:02:50,464
I hear it from my patients.

29
00:02:50,464 --> 00:02:55,700
Lots of people are tired of higher taxes.

30
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:58,678
I know,

31
00:02:58,678 --> 00:02:59,698
but if Boswell wins

32
00:02:59,698 --> 00:03:01,228
he'll be an important decision-maker

33
00:03:01,228 --> 00:03:02,431
on the school board,

34
00:03:02,431 --> 00:03:03,721
and he doesn't know anything

35
00:03:03,721 --> 00:03:06,034
about our children's education.

36
00:03:06,034 --> 00:03:07,612
Who's running against him?

37
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:10,589
Nobody. That's the problem.

38
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:12,742
Well, it sounds to me like Carter Boswell

39
00:03:12,742 --> 00:03:14,407
is going to win this seat on the board.

40
00:03:14,407 --> 00:03:16,545
Oh, not if I can stop him!

41
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:19,523
And how are you going to stop him?

42
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:22,501
I don't know.

43
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:27,257
Maybe I'll run against him.

44
00:03:27,257 --> 00:03:31,435
Well, you've got my vote.

45
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:35,413
I'm serious, Philip.

46
00:03:35,413 --> 00:03:37,391
Why shouldn't I run?

47
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:39,693
Why shouldn't you run for what, Mom?

48
00:03:39,693 --> 00:03:41,119
Your mother is thinking of

49
00:03:41,119 --> 00:03:43,347
running for the school board.

50
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:44,827
Hey, that's terrific, Mom!

51
00:03:44,827 --> 00:03:45,937
Against Carter Boswell?

52
00:03:45,937 --> 00:03:46,325
Great!

53
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:49,303
Well, if I run for office,

54
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:51,375
the voters will have a clear choice.

55
00:03:51,375 --> 00:03:55,259
I stand for everything Boswell doesn't.

56
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:57,759
I think a lot of people will vote for you

57
00:03:57,759 --> 00:03:58,757
against Boswell, Ellen.

58
00:03:58,757 --> 00:04:01,535
I'll vote for you.

59
00:04:01,535 --> 00:04:04,193
Will you help me if I do run?

60
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:05,193
Absolutely.

61
00:04:05,193 --> 00:04:06,050
The trouble is

62
00:04:06,050 --> 00:04:10,149
it takes a little bit of money to run a campaign.

63
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:12,149
I think you can make a difference, Ellen.

64
00:04:12,149 --> 00:04:13,667
And in a short campaign

65
00:04:13,667 --> 00:04:16,105
you wouldn't need as much money.

66
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:17,429
You know something, Ellen?

67
00:04:17,429 --> 00:04:21,003
Why not give the people of Riverdale a clear choice?

68
00:04:21,003 --> 00:04:22,060
I'm with you.

69
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:30,836
You can make a difference.

70
00:04:30,836 --> 00:04:33,972
Come in.

71
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:36,950
Mr. Maxwell?

72
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:40,915
Yes, Charles Maxwell.

73
00:04:40,915 --> 00:04:43,326
My name is Ellen Stewart.

74
00:04:43,326 --> 00:04:45,884
Hello.

75
00:04:45,884 --> 00:04:48,862
Please, sit down.

76
00:04:48,862 --> 00:04:51,840
You asked to see me.

77
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:55,568
What would you like to see me about?

78
00:04:55,568 --> 00:04:59,423
I'd like your help.

79
00:04:59,423 --> 00:05:00,236
Well,

80
00:05:00,236 --> 00:05:03,752
I'm editor of the most influential newspaper in Riverdale.

81
00:05:03,752 --> 00:05:06,730
Actually, it's the only newspaper.

82
00:05:06,730 --> 00:05:09,130
A lot of people would like my help.

83
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:09,708
Do you have a story?

84
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:14,366
I'm planning to run for the school board.

85
00:05:14,366 --> 00:05:15,664
Against Carter Boswell?

86
00:05:15,664 --> 00:05:16,664
Yes.

87
00:05:16,664 --> 00:05:18,642
Well, that is news.

88
00:05:18,642 --> 00:05:21,995
Will you announce that I'm running?

89
00:05:21,995 --> 00:05:24,598
But I need some information.

90
00:05:24,598 --> 00:05:27,576
Of course.

91
00:05:27,576 --> 00:05:30,764
Why will the voters vote for you against Boswell,

92
00:05:30,764 --> 00:05:31,184
Mrs. Stewart?

93
00:05:31,184 --> 00:05:36,509
Because I care.

94
00:05:36,509 --> 00:05:39,487
"Vote for Ellen Stewart. She cares."

95
00:05:39,487 --> 00:05:42,465
Not a bad slogan.

96
00:05:42,465 --> 00:05:45,443
But what do you care about?

97
00:05:45,443 --> 00:05:48,421
Well, I care about the children of our town.

98
00:05:48,421 --> 00:05:50,521
I don't want them to grow up

99
00:05:50,521 --> 00:05:52,269
without cultural programs in our school.

100
00:05:52,269 --> 00:05:56,377
Do you have a plan?

101
00:05:56,377 --> 00:05:58,342
I want our children to learn

102
00:05:58,342 --> 00:05:59,822
more than reading, writing, and arithmetic.

103
00:05:59,822 --> 00:06:03,311
I want to keep the after-school programs--

104
00:06:03,311 --> 00:06:04,811
the music, the concerts.

105
00:06:04,811 --> 00:06:09,267
It's not a bad plan.

106
00:06:09,267 --> 00:06:12,245
But who's going to pay for all of this?

107
00:06:12,245 --> 00:06:12,832
We are.

108
00:06:12,832 --> 00:06:14,885
The citizens of Riverdale, of course.

109
00:06:14,885 --> 00:06:18,201
I plan to get help

110
00:06:18,201 --> 00:06:21,179
That's fair enough.

111
00:06:21,179 --> 00:06:26,697
Exactly what do you want from me, Mrs. Stewart?

112
00:06:26,697 --> 00:06:27,682
You don't know me.

113
00:06:27,682 --> 00:06:31,749
I can't expect you to take my side against Boswell.

114
00:06:31,749 --> 00:06:33,978
But I do need some publicity

115
00:06:33,978 --> 00:06:37,084
so that the people of our town

116
00:06:37,084 --> 00:06:37,469
know that I'm running for office

117
00:06:37,469 --> 00:06:40,547
and that I care about our children.

118
00:06:40,547 --> 00:06:42,025
Fair enough.

119
00:06:42,025 --> 00:06:45,003
I certainly can print the news.

120
00:06:45,003 --> 00:06:48,003
And you are now making news.
